  "articleSummary": "The article argues that security agents should use model routers rather than rely on a single leaderboard ranking, because performance depends on task, tools, budget, latency, and evidence requirements. It presents ExploitHunter.app’s product-shaped evaluation suite—covering Juice Shop and Docker labs, network checks, planning, tool use, and system integration—and shows that cheap models can be effective, premium models may primarily buy speed, and local models can perform well with constrained tools. The analysis emphasizes behavior and infrastructure as much as final answers, including scope control, tool efficiency, evidence persistence, and failures caused by runners, providers, parsers, or evidence stores. Written in an analytical, engineering-focused tone, it repeatedly frames model selection as a cost-quality routing problem rather than a search for one universal winner.",
